{"title":"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest number in the set {<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c7b02d2797bbaa48be192cd9d839ab406b72b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.109, 0.2, 0.111, 0.114, 0.19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" />} is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21aa68ddb6205ad8747c480f2d41b96c3aad056a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 0.109 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 0.2 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 0.111 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 0.114 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 0.19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"464\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To figure out which number is largest, we look first at the number in the tenths position.  Since four of the given numbers have a 1 in the tenths position and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a270a7be617f39b92e4821298c4555cffe496c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a270a7be617f39b92e4821298c4555cffe496c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> is the\nlargest.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems